# Projects component error sentences.
error-code-branch-invalid = That branch name isn't allowed. Use "ordin/" followed by lower-case letters, numbers and hyphens.
error-code-commit-invalid = That starting point isn't valid. Choose a saved version from the list and try again.
error-code-group-too-small = A group of attempts needs at least two tasks on the same brief.
error-code-request-invalid = The description of the change is empty or too long. Shorten it and try again.
error-code-worktree-outside-root = That working folder is outside the place ordin keeps its files. Choose another folder.
error-cset-duplicate = This task already has a set of changes.
error-cset-hunk-too-large = One of the changes is too big to review here. Split it into smaller changes.
error-cset-undecided-entries = Some changes are still waiting for your decision. Decide on each one first.
error-ghop-above-ceiling = Your company's rules say this kind of action needs approval, so it can't be switched off.
error-ghop-duplicate = That action is already set up for this project.
error-gh-conflict = Someone changed that file or branch in the meantime. Refresh and try again.
error-gh-failed = The code host couldn't finish that. Try again in a moment.
error-gh-host-not-supported = ordin can't do that with this code host. Only GitHub and your company's GitLab are supported.
error-gh-not-found = That repository, file or proposed change wasn't found, or you can't see it.
error-gh-rate-limited = The code host is asking for a pause. Try again in a few minutes.
error-gh-sign-in-needed = Sign in to the code host first, then try again.
error-gh-unreachable = ordin can't reach the code host. Check your connection and try again.
error-lang-duplicate = That language is already in the list.
error-lang-server-not-approved = That language support isn't on your company's approved list. Choose an approved one.
error-lang-settings-invalid = The language settings aren't valid or are too large. Check them and try again.
error-proj-branch-exists = A branch with that name already exists. Choose another name.
error-proj-branch-mismatch = That project's current branch doesn't fit its set-up: only a project kept under version control has one.
error-proj-checks-invalid = A project can have at most 20 checks, each up to 1,000 characters. Shorten or remove some and try again.
error-proj-check-denied = That check wasn't allowed to run.
error-proj-check-timeout = That check ran for more than 30 minutes and was stopped. Try a shorter check.
error-proj-datastore-unavailable = ordin can't reach its project records right now. Try again in a moment.
error-proj-decision-invalid = That change can no longer be applied. Refresh the list and try again.
error-proj-entry-not-found = That change can no longer be found. Refresh the list and try again.
error-proj-files-failed = ordin couldn't save the files. Check there is room and try again.
error-proj-git-failed = The version-control step failed. Try again, and if it keeps failing, tell IT.
error-proj-ide-not-found = The editor wasn't found on this computer. Install it or choose another one.
error-proj-ide-start-failed = The editor wouldn't start. Try again.
error-proj-lsp-method-not-allowed = The editor asked for something ordin doesn't allow, so it was ignored.
error-proj-lsp-unavailable = Language support isn't available for this work right now. Turn it on in settings and try again.
error-proj-nothing-to-commit = There is nothing to save as a new version. Make a change first.
error-proj-not-a-repository = This folder isn't a project with version history. Choose another folder.
error-proj-not-found = That project wasn't found. It may have been removed.
error-proj-origin-changed = The shared copy changed since you opened these files. Refresh and try again.
error-proj-place-already-open = That place is already open as a project.
error-proj-push-refused = The shared copy refused your changes. You may not have permission, or the branch is protected. Update and try again.
error-proj-rate-limited = The code host is asking for a pause. Try again in a few minutes.
error-proj-remote-unreachable = ordin can't reach the shared copy. Check your connection and that the address is supported.
error-proj-server-install-failed = Language support couldn't be installed. Check your connection and try again.
error-proj-sign-in-needed = Sign in to GitHub or GitLab first, then try again.
error-proj-task-not-found = That task wasn't found.
error-proj-task-state-invalid = That can't be done to the task in its current state. Refresh and try again.
error-proj-terminal-failed = The terminal wouldn't start. Try again.
error-proj-too-many-attempts = That is more attempts than your company allows. Choose fewer.
error-proj-too-many-followed = You can follow up to 20 repositories. Stop following one first.
error-proj-undecided-changes = Some changes are still waiting for your decision. Decide on each one before saving.
error-proj-working-copy-dirty = Switching now would overwrite changes you haven't saved. Save or set them aside first.
error-proj-worktree-failed = ordin couldn't create or remove the working folder or branch. Try again.
